{
 "about": "Lower arch-cut sub-panel of the left door leaf of the Garden Gate (plate 4, 'North Side of Garden Gate'), left half, drawn by hand as smooth curves while viewing the University of Manchester copy of the 1786 engravings online (PR-CHCR-00457, image 26). Only these hand-drawn control points are used; no pixels of that scan. Coordinates are that scan's pixels. Curves are Catmull-Rom splines through the points; polylines are straight. The right half is the mirror image. Two ribbons end in curls at the outer side and meet a four-petal rosette with a central bead on the axis; the plain field around them is the ground, and the moulding along the bottom edge is raised.",
